Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:25:17 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 0/5] media: venus: make the HFI 1.x (MSM8916) encoder usable

The Venus encoder on MSM8916 (HFI 1.x, firmware VIDEO.VE.1.8) cannot be
used with current kernels: session setup fails on a property only newer
HFI versions know (patch 1). With that out of the way, GStreamer's
v4l2h264enc still made the firmware abort within the first frames,
because of three things the HFI 1.x firmware expects and the driver does
not provide: its own input buffer size (2), its own frame size as the
filled length (3), and no buffers added with VIDIOC_CREATE_BUFS while
streaming (4). Once encodes ran, the output was 4 to 14 times the target
bitrate, because the firmware budgets bits from the buffer timestamps,
which GStreamer uses as frame numbers (5).

Patches 1, 4 and 5 only change HFI 1.x. Patches 2 and 3 apply to all
encoder sessions, but they only ever raise a size to the value the
firmware itself reports; I could only test them on HFI 1.x.

Tested on a Samsung Galaxy Tab A 9.7 (SM-T550, APQ8016) with a kernel
based on msm8916-mainline 7.3-rc2, whose venus driver files are identical
to v7.3-rc6 apart from this series, using GStreamer 1.28.7
(videotestsrc ! v4l2h264enc), v4l2-ctl and GNOME Snapshot recording the
camera at 1152x864:
- before: VIDIOC_REQBUFS fails with -EINVAL; with patch 1 only, the
  firmware aborts ("Err_Fatal - venus/utils/src/vbuffer.c:1322") on the
  first frames; with patches 1-4, encodes run at 4-14x the target.
- after: 640x480 test bars 2.00 Mbit/s at a 2 Mbit/s VBR target, noise
  1.95 Mbit/s (2 Mbit/s CBR) and 8.14 Mbit/s (8 Mbit/s VBR), 1152x864
  bars 4.00 Mbit/s (4 Mbit/s VBR); no firmware errors.
Not tested: other HFI versions, and a plain mainline kernel.

Patch 1 returns -ENOTSUPP like the other properties hfi_cmds.c rejects,
since venus_session_set_property() skips exactly that error (checkpatch
suggests EOPNOTSUPP). The Fixes: commit ids were checked against
mainline; checkpatch cannot see them in my tree.

The fixes were developed with an AI assistant (see the Assisted-by
tags); I reviewed and tested them and take responsibility for them.

Yaron Shahrabani (5):
  media: venus: hfi_cmds: skip the H.264 8x8 transform property on HFI
    1.x
  media: venus: venc: honour the firmware input buffer size
  media: venus: helpers: report the full frame size for encoder input
  media: venus: venc: do not offer VIDIOC_CREATE_BUFS on HFI 1.x
  media: venus: venc: rate control from the frame rate on HFI 1.x

 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c  | 12 +++++
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c |  8 ++++
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c     | 47 ++++++++++++++++++--
